From: Vladimir <anykey196@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 04:20:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2w: add SDIO WiFi/BT (AW859A)

Enable the SDIO bus (mmc1) and power the on-board AW859A (UWE5622)
WiFi/BT combo through an mmc-pwrseq-simple that resets WL_REG_ON (PG18)
and gates the RTC 32 kHz fanout clock (PG10).

The pwrseq clock must be named "ext_clock" (what mmc-pwrseq-simple
requests) and its output pin must be muxed to the clock function, as
done for the other H616/H618 boards.

Tested on: OrangePi Zero 2W (Allwinner H618) with the out-of-tree
uwe5622 driver.

Signed-off-by: Vladimir <anykey196@gmail.com>
---
Note: unlike v3, this revision does not add separate fixed regulators:
VCC-WIFI is the existing 3.3V reg_vcc3v3 rail and VCC-WIFI-IO is the
AXP313A aldo1 rail, as suggested in review by Andre Przywara. Change
made locally while carrying the patch in ImmortalWrt.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
@@ -189,3 +189,25 @@
 	usb1_vbus-supply = <&reg_vcc5v>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/ {
+	wifi_pwrseq: wifi-pwrseq {
+		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
+		clocks = <&rtc CLK_OSC32K_FANOUT>;
+		clock-names = "ext_clock";
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&x32clk_fanout_pin>;
+		reset-gpios = <&pio 6 18 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PG18 */
+		post-power-on-delay-ms = <200>;
+	};
+};
+
+&mmc1 {
+	vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
+	bus-width = <4>;
+	non-removable;
+	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
+	status = "okay";
+};
